  "findings": [
    "Only old loader is removed from existing per-frame clutter chain; other systems and registrations are preserved. This deletion is necessary with real 61-asset loader, not a per-frame preload.",
    "Gameplay Startup closure requires the same App AssetMeshLibrary, MeshWatch and GameConfig, captures explicit installed root, calls reviewed leaf v2, inserts actual canonical catalog only after full producer returns through Commands.",
    "Registration marker deduplicates installer only. GameplayApplication marks actual gameplay World role at real constructor and direct gameplay GPU installer; loading App is independently new and does not copy this role. Neither marker stands for completion.",
    "Worker checks canonical catalog immediately after successful real SubApp.update before LoadingGameComplete/warmup. Synchronous driver catches actual App.update unwind into Err, then checks actual role/catalog before GUI output/render/success progress. State/Camera absence does not bypass gate.",
    "Assets remain per same actual World across SubApp handoff. Missing/invalid asset panic is visible; partial original CPU/watch side effects are not rolled back or called success. Existing owner/save disposal is reused.",
    "No early catalog insertion, generated geometry, default catalog, fake Ready event, added schedule barrier, or complete plugin install. Existing Nani PreStartup placement is preserved; atlas binding and remaining original startup tuple members remain separate incomplete consumers.",
    "Workspace system-clutter exists but tiny-glade package did not declare it. Required root-only system-clutter.workspace=true is explicitly recorded; package build is not claimed by source parser."
  ],
